https://github.com/mozilla/readability
Copyright (c) 2010 Arc90 Inc, and subsequent contributors.

The crate `legibility-legacy` is a Rust port of Readability.js's `parse()` pipeline.
It is a derivative work of mozilla/readability and is therefore covered by that
project's Apache License 2.0. This is why the entire legibility workspace is licensed
Apache-2.0: matching the upstream license removes any compatibility question.

`legibility-legacy` exists as a conformance ORACLE, not as a product feature. It lets a
parity failure be attributed to one of three causes -- a defect in our arena/serializer
(INFRA), a difference between html5ever and jsdom tree construction (PARSER), or a
floating-point near-tie selecting a different top candidate (ARITH). Without it, every
early failure is indistinguishable from every other.

The corpus under corpus/readability/ is a git submodule of mozilla/readability, pinned by
commit SHA. Its test-pages fixtures remain under that project's license and are not
redistributed by this repository.

