dom_smoothie  (MIT License)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
https://github.com/niklak/dom_smoothie
Copyright (c) 2024 Mykola Humanov

Portions of `legibility-legacy` -- specifically the transcription of Readability.js's
scoring arithmetic, word lists, comma table, title-separator table, metadata key tables
and URL helpers into Rust idiom -- were informed by dom_smoothie's existing transcription
of the same upstream algorithm. Files containing such portions carry an attribution header
naming the dom_smoothie source file.

dom_smoothie is additionally used as a second differential baseline in the parity harness
(see docs/parity-gate.md). It is an observation point, not an authority: several
deliberate divergences from Readability.js are registered as expected divergences rather
than failures, most notably `min_score_to_adjust` (default 5.0), which causes candidates
scoring at or below 5.0 to skip link-density normalization entirely.

